      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Primary headache, such as migraine and tension type headache is a common symptom in patients presenting in emergency departments. Suspicious of secondary headache is a medical history of new onset, changing character of a previously known headache, resistancy to medication or symptoms which are not typical of primary headache."},
